# ARCHITECTURE OPTIMIZATION RULES (Maintainability-First)

## Core principle

- Prefer maintainability and correctness over micro-optimizations.
- Use the existing folder structure rules (`folder-structure.mdc`).

## AI Response Quality Rules (Less fluff, more precision)

### Output style

- Be brief & precise. Prefer 3–7 bullets over paragraphs.
- Answer first, then details (only if needed).
- Use user language (RU/EN). No mixed languages unless required.
- No filler, no repeating the user’s text.

### Clarifying questions (mandatory)

- Ask 1–3 questions before coding/executing if: target (URL/file/function) unclear, expected vs current unclear, secrets/PII involved, env constraints unknown.
- If proceeding with an assumption, state it in 1 line.

### Decision discipline

- Prefer repo evidence over guesses (search/read first if unsure).
- One coherent approach (no multiple options unless asked).
- Risky changes → safe fallback + backwards-compatible default.
- Never invent tool/test/external outputs.

### Token efficiency (without losing quality)

- No repetition. Summarize big context as top-N. Prefer compact structured formats.

### Safety

- Never output/log secrets. Redact. Validate inputs. No hardcoded keys/tokens.

